 "captions": [
  {
   "start": 0,
   "end": 1.02,
   "text": "Hour six."
  },
  {
   "start": 1.53,
   "end": 2.86,
   "text": "The grid is still down."
  },
  {
   "start": 3.45,
   "end": 5.44,
   "text": "Your fridge just passed its four-hour mark."
  },
  {
   "start": 5.99,
   "end": 6.99,
   "text": "The USDA rule:"
  },
  {
   "start": 7.42,
   "end": 11.37,
   "text": "if milk, meat or eggs sit above 40\u00b0F for more than two hours..."
  },
  {
   "start": 11.82,
   "end": 12.4,
   "text": "throw them out."
  },
  {
   "start": 13.0,
   "end": 14.75,
   "text": "Your freezer is your best friend now."
  },
  {
   "start": 15.17,
   "end": 17.32,
   "text": "A full one holds for about 48 hours."
  },
  {
   "start": 17.71,
   "end": 18.22,
   "text": "Half full?"
  },
  {
   "start": 18.58,
   "end": 19.35,
   "text": "Just 24."
  },
  {
   "start": 19.9,
   "end": 21.55,
   "text": "Cell signal starts to vanish."
  },
  {
   "start": 21.96,
   "end": 26.13,
   "text": "Industry guidelines call for as little as four hours of backup power at many sites."
  },
  {
   "start": 26.58,
   "end": 28.15,
   "text": "That time... is running out."
  },
  {
   "start": 28.68,
   "end": 30.14,
   "text": "Every traffic light is dark."
  },
  {
   "start": 30.52,
   "end": 34.02,
   "text": "In most states, that turns every intersection into an all-way stop."
  },
  {
   "start": 34.44,
   "end": 35.47,
   "text": "Your tap still works."
  },
  {
   "start": 35.77,
   "end": 39.6,
   "text": "Water towers push water down with gravity, and many hold about a day's supply."
  },
  {
   "start": 40.02,
   "end": 42.08,
   "text": "But the pumps that refill them need power."
  },
  {
   "start": 42.51,
   "end": 43.56,
   "text": "And at hour twelve..."
  },
  {
   "start": 44.01,
   "end": 45.51,
   "text": "your phone becomes the problem."
  },
  {
   "start": 46.16,
   "end": 47.36,
   "text": "Follow for part three."
  }
 ]
}